Tokyo NRT
If landing at terminal 1 (T1) might be confusing (At the middle of the U shape is the visitor service center) (On the U extensions approximately at 50% length [inwards] are the exits)
If landing at terminal 2 (T2) very simple (small section)
If landing at terminal 3, walk to terminal 2

Go to visitor service center and use “7/11 atms” to extract some cash 10,000 yen ($62) (always extract yen, you incur a charge extracting other conversions)

Find the “JR East Travel Service Centre” and subscribe to their mailing list and get a “Free Sakura Keychain”
Get a free “Welcome Suica Card”, just show passport


Trains are located in basement (B1)
